[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066612777","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108557#issuecomment-3066612777","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108557","id":3066612777,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62yMwp","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-13T05:24:35Z","updated_at":"2025-07-13T05:24:35Z","body":"I pushed a new solution which, I think, is much better than previous one. This doesn't set the system bars to black instead checks the background color luminance and set the icon appearance accordingly. This means that any color set by the user using `android:windowBackground`  would be preserved and godot would make sure system bar icons are visible on that color.\r\n\r\nNote: This PR should be tested with changes from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108287","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066612777/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3071838846","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108557#issuecomment-3071838846","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108557","id":3071838846,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc63GIp-","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-15T04:22:40Z","updated_at":"2025-07-15T07:34:30Z","body":"I've converted this to draft for now. Let's first finalize https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108287 . Both PRs are touching window management code so, it's hard to work on in parallel.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3071838846/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3091924304","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108557#issuecomment-3091924304","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108557","id":3091924304,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64SwVQ","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-19T06:09:23Z","updated_at":"2025-07-19T06:09:23Z","body":"> Test on Android 13, only this PR without #108287\r\n> \r\n> * `Immersive mode`  = `disabled`\r\n> * `Edge To Edge` = `disabled`\r\n> \r\n> But the app is still forced in `edge-to-edge` mode. When I try to display the system notifications/functions as in the video, or press the `Home/Task` button and bring the app back, the app is suddenly correct (no edge-to-edge mode).\r\n> \r\n> **EDIT:** I was able to reproduce this behavior as in the video with this PR + #108287 (Cherry-pick) in a new local test branch.\r\n\r\nI couldn’t reproduce it on Android 11 or 15. I had pushed a minor fix in #108287 after you tested this PR, which addressed a somewhat similar issue on Android 9. Could you try testing it again now and see if the issue still persists?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3091924304/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3105731422","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108557#issuecomment-3105731422","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108557","id":3105731422,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65HbNe","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-23T05:23:52Z","updated_at":"2025-07-23T05:27:09Z","body":"Evaluating `GradientDrawable` is one option and this code to get color from gradient seems good too.\r\n\r\nHowever, I'm considering a different approach now. I want to add a export setting `root window color` that would set the `android:windowBackground` (Black as default) and we'd make this a reserved attribute. That way we'd already have the background color and we can then set system bar appearance. This approach is simple and ensure that system bar is always visible for godot apps. It would solve the regression and would also be a good enahancement.\r\n\r\n@m4gr3d @Alex2782 Thought?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3105731422/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3106367735","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108557#issuecomment-3106367735","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108557","id":3106367735,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65J2j3","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-23T07:59:15Z","updated_at":"2025-07-23T08:10:39Z","body":"> However, I'm considering a different approach now. I want to add a export setting `root window color` that would set the `android:windowBackground` (Black as default) and we'd make this a reserved attribute.\r\n\r\nSounds like a better solution. What about Gradle builds? \r\nI don't know all the details, but from what I've seen, many people use some kind of custom style (at least that's my impression)\r\n\r\nI think we'll have to continue evaluating theme/styles, like the current one already does.\r\n\r\n-----------\r\n\r\n`return if (theme.resolveAttribute(android.R.attr.windowBackground, typedValue, true) && typedValue.type in TypedValue.TYPE_FIRST_COLOR_INT..TypedValue.TYPE_LAST_COLOR_INT)\r\n`\r\n\r\n`07-22 18:57:15.816  6974  6974 D Godot   : typedValue.type: 3`\r\n\r\nIn my case `TYPE_STRING` (I think it was) was determined here (apk export)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3106367735/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3106554588","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108557#issuecomment-3106554588","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108557","id":3106554588,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65KkLc","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-23T08:44:26Z","updated_at":"2025-07-23T08:44:26Z","body":"> What about Gradle builds?\r\nI don't know all the details, but from what I've seen, many people use some kind of custom style (at least that's my impression)\r\n>\r\n> I think we'll have to continue evaluating theme/styles, like the current one already does.\r\n\r\nWe'd add  `android:windowBackground` to reserved attribute so folks won't be able to override it using `Custom Theme Attributes` option and `GodotAppMainTheme` is also generated during export so manually overwriting that is also not possible. `root window color` would be only option to change the window background.\r\n\r\nWe won't need to evaluate the theme because we can get the color directly from export setting and set appearance accordingly.\r\n\r\nIf user replaces the `GodotAppMainTheme` with a custom style, or set a window background programmatically on Android side, then it's their job to setting the appearance accordingly (as they'd do for a normal android apps) and they should override the `setSystemBarsAppearance` method.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3106554588/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3117564046","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108557#issuecomment-3117564046","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108557","id":3117564046,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc650kCO","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-25T12:15:12Z","updated_at":"2025-07-25T12:15:12Z","body":"Added an export setting to configure the window background color.\r\n\r\nOn non-Gradle builds, the color is applied after a slight delay, as it's set during app launch.\r\nOn Gradle builds, the color is set in the app theme (android:windowBackground) during export, so there's no delay.\r\n\r\nWhen determining the window background color to set the system bar appearance, logic first checks if the window background is a ColorDrawable and retrieves its color. If it's not a ColorDrawable, it falls back to the color defined in the export setting.\r\n\r\nWhile this may seem redundant, it's intentional. This approach ensures that if the window background color is changed at runtime, Godot will use that updated color when applying system bar appearance during app resume, instead of reverting to the export-time color.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3117564046/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3130154951","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108557#issuecomment-3130154951","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108557","id":3130154951,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66kl_H","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-28T23:56:27Z","updated_at":"2025-07-28T23:56:27Z","body":"> Whitespace needs trimming\r\n\r\nMaybe we can use it to check Kotlin files? \r\n\r\n- https://pinterest.github.io/ktlint/latest/\r\n- https://github.com/detekt/detekt\r\n\r\nI've always assumed that different standards apply to Kotlin; GHA `Static checks / Code style` have so far only rejected it for C++.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments